&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is Procurement at Lattice&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lattice’s Procurement Team builds value for the company through both supplier and stakeholder relationships and balanced agreements. As part of the accounting team, we place a large focus on risk mitigation and compliance in addition to the commercial elements of the deals we support. We are a small team with a huge impact on Lattice’s future success.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contract details: This is a two-month contract role, fully remote, 3 days/week guaranteed with the potential for additional hours as needed. You’ll have the opportunity to gain hands-on experience with the full procurement lifecycle, procurement orchestration tools (P2P), and exposure to a high-performing tech organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ll be responsible for reviewing, scoping, negotiating, and executing procurement requests from intake through signature.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ll partner with cross-functional leaders, stakeholders, and department contacts from FP&amp;amp;A, Finance, IT, Security, Compliance, Privacy, and Legal to ensure our deals meet or exceed team requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ll provide consultation before, during, and after deal cycles to our internal teams, ensuring that we purchase the right things and get exceptional value from our suppliers and partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Bring to the Table&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3 years of experience with commercial negotiations, procurement initiatives, or complex vendor engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong understanding of SaaS procurement, services agreements, and supplier relationships, along with hands-on experience using procurement orchestration tools, ideally Zip.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail to ensure clean and accurate records within Lattice systems reflecting up-to-date deal statuses, vendor records, and intake reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, thoughtful communication skills, with the ability to adapt your approach based on audience and situation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
