&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lattice’s Engineering team is building the future of People + AI. We’re reimagining our talent management suite – including Reviews, Surveys, and Goals – with AI-powered experiences that unlock capabilities and insights that would otherwise be impossible to deliver. Our products help organizations surface meaningful signals, make better-informed decisions, and ultimately improve the performance outcomes their people and businesses rely on every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Talent Engineering organization is at the forefront of this evolution. They build the best-in-class suite of products across Performance Management, Engagement Surveys, and Goal Setting, helping shape how organizations develop their people and achieve their goals at a time when AI is redefining what’s possible in talent management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the Talent Engineering organization, spanning 50+ engineers and managers across a portfolio of customer-facing products. Making thoughtful tradeoffs across customer needs, product priorities, and engineering investment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and develop engineering managers and senior leaders across Lattice Engineering while continuing to raise the bar for leadership, execution, and organizational health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure a delightful, reliable experience for Lattice customers around the globe while simultaneously enabling a rapid pace of product development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with our Product and Design partners to define, plan, and prioritize our product strategy and roadmap that translates into outcomes for customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Lattice in conversations with key prospects and customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with the broader Engineering leadership team to shape department-wide strategy and goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale the systems, processes, and organizational practices that enable multiple teams to plan effectively, deliver reliably, and learn quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You Will Bring to the Table&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of engineering management experience, including at least 5 years leading an engineering organization composed of multiple teams and multiple layers of leadership.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing engineering investment across a portfolio of products and making thoughtful tradeoffs when resources are constrained.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A history of shipping high-quality products where quality, trust, reliability, and scalability are essential to customer success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A high degree of autonomy, ownership, and sound judgment, with the ability to operate with a CEO mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to develop engineering leaders, including both individual contributors and managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An eye for great products and the ability to work cross-functionally to effectively deliver them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and executive presence, with the ability to influence decisions across Engineering, Product, Design, and company leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity about AI and its potential to improve how organizations develop their people.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
