&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Come join us on our mission to build cultures where employees and companies thrive. We’re looking for a detail-oriented Staff Accountant to help maintain accurate, timely, and scalable financial operations. You will own key accounting processes, support the monthly close, improve controls and documentation, and partner with cross-functional teams across the business to turn operational activity into reliable financial reporting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for an experienced accountant who is highly organized, comfortable working independently within established processes, and motivated to identify practical improvements as the business grows and changes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own commission and bonus accounting, including calculation review, monthly accruals, related account reconciliations, and coordination with FP&amp;amp;A and Payroll teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Account for capitalized commissions in accordance with applicable accounting guidance, including amortization, reconciliations, and supporting schedules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own key accounting areas, including cash, prepaids, fixed assets, and intercompany accounting, as applicable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure transactions are recorded in accordance with company accounting policies and US GAAP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Accounts Payable, Payroll, FP&amp;amp;A, and operational teams to ensure complete and timely financial information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with audit, tax, and compliance requests by preparing clear schedules and supporting documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain organized accounting records, process documentation, and internal control evidence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify recurring issues or manual workarounds and recommend improvements to processes, controls, and systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI and automation to improve close workflows, reporting, and analysis, reducing manual work, increasing accuracy, and scaling the function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to ad hoc reporting, analysis, and special projects as the business evolves&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Bring to the Table&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5+ years of progressive accounting experience; public accounting and/or high-growth company experience is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
